# High-Society Hunter: "Whenever this creature attacks, you may sacrifice another creature. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on this
# creature. Whenever another nontoken creature dies, draw a card." Bot1 casts it on turn 1 with Black Lotus and two Moxen; on
# turn 3 it attacks and Bot1 sacrifices its Memnite to the trigger (one creature only, not both it and the Ornithopter, and not the Hunter itself): the Hunter gets one counter (CR 122.1, 6/4 - not 7/5) and
# the Memnite's death, a nontoken creature other than the Hunter, draws a card (CR 700.4); the 6 damage in the air is 6.

